# WriteProperty and WritePropertyMultiple (§15.9, §15.10), and how they fail.

# present-value 42.5 at priority 8; the same without a priority; and the
# relinquish — NULL at the same priority — that gives the slot back.
00 05 01 0f 0c 00 40 00 01 19 55 3e 44 42 2a 00 00 3f 49 08 => write-property analog-output:1 present-value = real 42.5 priority 8
00 05 03 0f 0c 00 40 00 01 19 55 3e 44 42 2a 00 00 3f => write-property analog-output:1 present-value = real 42.5
00 05 04 0f 0c 00 40 00 01 19 55 3e 00 3f 49 08 => write-property analog-output:1 present-value = null priority 8
00 05 02 0f 0c 00 80 00 01 19 4d 3e 75 04 00 46 61 6e 3f => write-property analog-value:1 object-name = string "Fan"
00 05 05 0f 0c 00 40 00 01 19 57 29 08 3e 44 42 70 00 00 3f => write-property analog-output:1 priority-array index 8 = real 60.0
# Two objects in one request.
00 05 06 10 0c 00 80 00 01 1e 09 55 2e 44 3f 80 00 00 2f 09 4d 2e 75 04 00 46 61 6e 2f 1f 0c 00 40 00 01 1e 09 55 2e 44 42 2a 00 00 2f 39 08 1f => write-property-multiple analog-value:1 present-value = real 1.0, object-name = string "Fan"; analog-output:1 present-value = real 42.5 priority 8
# Refused: write-access-denied (40); and the multiple write that names the
# first write it could not make.
50 07 0f 91 02 91 28 => error write-property: property: write-access-denied
50 08 10 0e 91 02 91 28 0f 1e 0c 00 80 00 01 19 4d 1f => write-property-multiple-error property: write-access-denied at analog-value:1 object-name
# A write with no value.
00 05 09 0f 0c 00 40 00 01 19 55 => error missing-field 3
